      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 70-year-old male sustained a Jefferson burst fracture with unilateral vertebral artery dissection and occlusion by displaced fragments. We performed reduction and posterior C1-ring osteosynthesis. We present a description of the intraoperative manual assessment of atlantoaxial stability. The vertebral artery was found with a good anterograde flow posteroperatively, and MRA showed reperfusion of the vessel. The patient was free of pain with preserved C1-C2 rotation after 6 weeks. Function-preserving posterior C1-ring osteosynthesis after reduction in a displaced Jefferson burst fracture complicated by vertebral artery dissection and occlusion may restore blood flow."},
